    {
      "title": "Explicit, new and Arrow Binding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Explicit, new and Arrow Binding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. call, apply, bind",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Runs",
                "Args"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`fn.call(ctx, a, b)`",
                  "now",
                  "one by one"
                ],
                [
                  "`fn.apply(ctx, [a, b])`",
                  "now",
                  "one array"
                ],
                [
                  "`fn.bind(ctx, a)`",
                  "later, returns a **NEW** fn",
                  "partial args"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`this = ctx` for that call",
                "`bind` does ==not run== the function",
                "Bound `this` is ==permanent==: a second bind or call cannot change it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. new and arrows",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Empty object",
                    "sub": "linked to `Fn.prototype`",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run Fn",
                    "sub": "`this` = that object",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Return it",
                    "sub": "unless Fn returns another object",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Arrows have no own ==this==, `arguments` or `prototype`",
                "`this` is captured **lexically** from the enclosing scope",
                "call/apply/bind cannot rebind an arrow; `new` {red:throws}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: lost this",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "setTimeout(obj.method, 0);            // this lost",
                "setTimeout(obj.method.bind(obj), 0);  // fix 1",
                "setTimeout(() => obj.method(), 0);    // fix 2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Why it breaks",
              "text": "`obj.method` passed bare is a plain function: no `obj.` at call time, so ==default binding==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Prototype Chain Internals",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Prototype Chain Internals",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Lookup Chain",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Every object has an internal ==[[Prototype]]==, read with `Object.getPrototypeOf(o)`",
                "Lookup walks ==o==, then its prototype, up to `Object.prototype`, then `null`",
                "Not found anywhere gives {red:undefined}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "obj",
                    "sub": "own props",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fn.prototype",
                    "sub": "shared",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Object.prototype",
                    "sub": "toString...",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "null",
                    "sub": "undefined",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Links, Writes, Create",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Fn.prototype` becomes the [[Prototype]] of `new Fn()` objects",
                "`obj.__proto__` is the ==legacy accessor== to the same link",
                "**Writes** go on the object and ==shadow== the prototype; **reads** fall through",
                "`Object.create(proto)` sets the prototype; `Object.create(null)` gives a chainless ==dictionary==",
                "`Object.getPrototypeOf(new Fn()) === Fn.prototype`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "function Fn() {}",
                "Fn.prototype.x = 1;",
                "const a = new Fn();",
                "a.x = 2;",
                "console.log(Object.getPrototypeOf(a) === Fn.prototype, a.x, Fn.prototype.x);",
                "console.log(Object.hasOwn(a, 'toString'), 'toString' in a, a instanceof Fn);"
              ],
              "note": "write shadows, prototype keeps 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "true 2 1",
                "false true true"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Checking Properties",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Check",
                "Looks at"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`hasOwnProperty(k)` / `Object.hasOwn(o, k)`",
                  "{green:own only}"
                ],
                [
                  "`k in obj`",
                  "own + {blue:inherited}"
                ],
                [
                  "`a instanceof Fn`",
                  "is `Fn.prototype` in a's chain?"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Classes as Sugar over Prototypes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Classes as Sugar over Prototypes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What class Really Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`class A { m() {} }` puts `m` on ==A.prototype==: shared, non-enumerable",
                "`constructor` is the **function body** of `A`",
                "`typeof A === 'function'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. extends and super",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "extends sets two links",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "B.prototype",
                    "note": "[[Prototype]] = A.prototype",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "B",
                    "note": "[[Prototype]] = A",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Second link means ==static methods inherit== too",
                "Derived constructor: `super(...)` **before** `this`",
                "Otherwise {red:ReferenceError}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Not Quite Plain Functions",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "function",
                "class"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Call without `new`",
                  "runs",
                  "{red:TypeError}"
                ],
                [
                  "Strict mode",
                  "sloppy default",
                  "**always**"
                ],
                [
                  "Hoisting",
                  "usable early",
                  "TDZ"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Field `handle = () => {...}` is an ==own property==, per instance",
                "Not on the prototype; the usual fix for lost `this`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "class Btn {",
                "  handle = () => this.label",
                "  m() {}",
                "}",
                "Object.hasOwn(new Btn(), 'handle') // true",
                "Object.hasOwn(new Btn(), 'm')      // false"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A class is a constructor function plus methods on `.prototype`. Arrow fields cost one function **per instance**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common this Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common this Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Lost binding",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const f = obj.method; f()` loses ==implicit binding==",
                "Falls to {red:default}: `undefined` in strict mode, so `this.x` throws TypeError",
                "`arr.forEach(function(){ this })` also gets ==default binding==",
                "Fix: an **arrow function**, or pass `thisArg`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "const f = obj.method;",
                "f();                    // TypeError",
                "arr.forEach(function (x) {",
                "  this.add(x);",
                "}, this);               // thisArg"
              ],
              "note": "thisArg is the second argument of forEach"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Arrow and bind traps",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Why",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`{ hi: () => this.name }`",
                  "Arrow takes **outer** `this`, not the object",
                  "Method `hi() {}`"
                ],
                [
                  "`addEventListener('click', fn.bind(o))`",
                  "`bind` returns a ==new function== each time",
                  "Keep a reference"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. new and prototypes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No `new`: sloppy mode sets properties on the ==global object==",
                "`Fn.prototype.list = []` is **shared** by all instances",
                "Put per-instance state in the constructor"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Ask at the call",
              "text": "new? call/apply/bind? `obj.`? plain? Arrows ignore all four."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
